  "details": "Invite responses are a very useful feature, and I believe that they carry a formal and personal touch of communication from user-to-user.\n\nPlayers can choose to respond to an invite, but can also choose to ignore the invite and letting the invite expire after fifteen minutes. No notification is given to the requester.\n\nIt would be neat if I could receive a generated reply if my invite is pending for fifteen minutes, and received no response.\n\nExample notification: \"Sorry that I haven't responded to your invite! I might either be AFK, logged out already, or got really busy. Let's hang out another time.\"",
